<section class="lab-hero" aria-labelledby="lab-title">
  <p class="mono-label">SEO inventory stress test · browser-local</p><h1
    id="lab-title"
  >
    Test the assumption that changes the page action.
  </h1><p>
    The same topic can need a section, a wider update, a merge, a new URL or no
    work at all. Compare inventory states without calling an AI provider.
  </p>
</section>
<section class="decision-lab" aria-labelledby="stress-title">
  <div class="stress-controls">
    <h2 id="stress-title">Decision stress test</h2><p>
      Set the topic and evidence state. The table holds those inputs constant
      and varies only the page inventory.
    </p><label for="stress-topic">Keyword or page question</label><input
      id="stress-topic"
      maxlength="160"
      value="How to choose a project management tool"
    /><label for="stress-evidence">Evidence on hand</label><select
      id="stress-evidence"
      ><option value="none">No evidence collected</option><option
        value="secondary">Secondary sources only</option
      ><option value="primary" selected>Primary or firsthand evidence</option
      ><option value="observed">Observed data or reproducible test</option
      ></select
    ><button class="primary-button" id="run-stress-test" type="button"
      >Update matrix</button
    ><p class="lab-privacy">
      Nothing is sent or retained. This is a deterministic sensitivity check,
      not an AI evaluation.
    </p>
  </div><div class="stress-results">
    <p class="mono-label">One variable changed · page inventory</p><h2>
      Six inventory states
    </h2><div id="stress-grid" class="stress-grid" aria-live="polite"></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="lab-method" aria-labelledby="lab-method-title">
  <div>
    <h2 id="lab-method-title">What this lab is for</h2><p>
      Use it when a recommendation feels too dependent on an unverified
      assumption about the current site.
    </p>
  </div><dl>
    <div>
      <dt>Hold constant</dt><dd>
        The topic, primary user job and evidence readiness.
      </dd>
    </div><div>
      <dt>Change</dt><dd>
        Whether a page exists, the size of its gap, overlap and inventory
        certainty.
      </dd>
    </div><div>
      <dt>Observe</dt><dd>
        Which assumption flips the recommended page action.
      </dd>
    </div><div>
      <dt>Then verify</dt><dd>
        Inspect the real URLs before acting. A matrix is not a crawl.
      </dd>
    </div>
  </dl><p class="lab-boundary">
    This lab does not compare AI-provider answers. For public-answer evidence
    work, use <a href="https://ai-fanout.com/lab/" rel="external">AI Fanout</a>,
    which shares the same operator and is not independent corroboration.
  </p><a class="text-link" href="/tool/"
    >Make the final page decision <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
</section>
<script>
  import "../scripts/decision-lab";
</script>
